What is Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF)?
---RESPONSE---
Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) is a technique used in information retrieval to combine ranked lists from multiple sources (e.g., search engines) into a single, more effective ranking. It works by taking the reciprocal of the rank position of each item across all sources and summing these values, with lower ranks (higher relevance) contributing more significantly. This approach aims to improve diversity and robustness in combined results.

